sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant T as Team computer<br/>fetch_snapshot.py,<br/>build_game_data.py
  participant A as ARGUS API<br/>api.argusservices.athenarc.gr
  participant P as Raspberry Pi<br/>guardian_live.py (systemd timer)
  participant C as Raspberry Pi<br/>Caddy + playit tunnel
  participant G as GitHub Actions<br/>site.yml
  participant W as GitHub Pages<br/>(HTTPS)
  participant B as Player's browser<br/>Aegis

  rect rgb(255, 246, 238)
    Note over T,A: A. Snapshot, once per data update (by hand)
    loop for each of 12 resources (assets, asset-states, threats, threat-contexts, events, policies, installed-instruments, installed-devices, instruments, instrument-types, decisions, decision-contexts)
      loop page = 1 … meta.last_page
        T->>A: GET /api/{resource}?page={page}  [Accept: application/json]
        A-->>T: 200 {data: [15 records], meta: {last_page, total}}
        Note right of T: 0.25 s pause · network error: up to 4 tries, waiting 2, 4, 6 s
      end
      Note over T: de-duplicate by id · complete = count ≥ meta.total · write snapshot_DATE/{resource}.json
    end
    Note over T: build_game_data.py: analysis (see data-analysis) → game_data.json · git push to main
  end

  rect rgb(240, 247, 244)
    Note over P,A: B. Live data, every 2 hours
    loop resource in (threat-contexts, events)
      loop from the page read last time, at most 400 pages
        P->>A: GET /api/{resource}?page={page}
        A-->>P: 200 {data, meta: {last_page, total}}
        Note right of P: keep records with id > last id read · 0.5 s pause · 3 tries, 30 s timeout
      end
      alt meta.total shrank (ARGUS replaced records)
        Note over P: forget that resource and read it again from page 1
      end
    end
    Note over P: state.json: read position, latest check of each danger, 10 newest AD-RT alarms per monument
    alt the run succeeded
      Note over P: write argus-now.json (schema 1, about 22 KB)
    else ARGUS unreachable or an error
      Note over P: keep the last good argus-now.json, try again in 2 hours
    end
  end

  rect rgb(238, 243, 251)
    Note over G,W: C. Build and publish, on every push to main and every night at 23:00 UTC
    G->>G: data tests (Python) · web tests (Vitest) · build (TypeScript check + Vite)
    G->>C: GET /live/argus-now.json  [HTTP via playit]
    alt 200 and JSON with schema 1 and sites
      C-->>G: argus-now.json
    else Pi unreachable or the file is not valid
      Note over G: take live/argus-now.json from the site branch (the last build’s copy), or publish without it
    end
    G->>W: force-push one commit to the site branch (built app, data, live file, VERSION)
    Note over W: GitHub Pages serves the site branch over HTTPS
  end

  rect rgb(246, 240, 251)
    Note over W,B: D. A player opens the game
    B->>W: GET / (index.html, JavaScript, styles)  [HTTPS]
    W-->>B: 200 · the service worker keeps an offline copy
    B->>W: GET data/game_data.json  (network first, offline copy if no network)
    W-->>B: 200 monuments, dangers, alarms, levels
    B->>W: GET live/argus-now.json  (at most every 10 min, 8 s timeout)
    alt file present and valid
      W-->>B: 200 · "Live from ARGUS": checks ≤ 14 days old, alarms ≤ 2 months old
    else missing, late or invalid
      Note over B: the live box is not shown, the game plays as usual
    end
    opt the 3D view is opened
      B->>W: GET data/view3d/{scene}.json, model (glTF, Draco), terrain
      Note over B: plus satellite and elevation tiles and Wikimedia photos from their own servers
    end
  end
